      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Clinical diagnosis of neurosarcoidosis depends on the finding of neurological disease in a patient with biopsy proven multisystem sarcoidosis. Without the biopsy evidence, solitary central nervous system sarcoidosis remains a difficult diagnosis. In some cases, only a long-term follow-up will establish the diagnosis."},
